# Cargo's build output. Nothing here is written by hand.
target

# The compiled TypeScript surface, produced from packages/*/src.
dist

# Installed packages, formatted by whoever published them.
node_modules

# Coverage reports, regenerated by `just coverage` on every run.

# Golden scenes and the images they must produce. The JSON is machine-written,
# so reformatting it rewrites every fixture and turns the next real change into
# a diff nobody can read.
fixtures

# meo-skia-canvas's JavaScript layer, carried here and repointed at this
# repository's binary. It is written in that project's style -- double quotes,
# semicolons, eighty columns -- and formatting it to this one's rewrites all
# 7,861 lines. That diff is what upstream is read against: it is how a fix
# released there is found and applied here, and how the two copies are checked
# against each other. Reformatting buys consistency in files nobody edits and
# spends the only tool there is for keeping them in step.
packages/*/vendor

# Emitted from the Rust property tables by `just gen-arena-tables`, so the
# generator and prettier would disagree about a file neither of them owns --
# and the regenerate-and-diff check would then fail on formatting rather than
# on drift. Same reason the vendored tree is excluded.
packages/*/src/generated

# Chrome measurement tables, written by the conformance harness in
# `tools/conformance/` and read back by the Rust tests. Machine-written, like
# the fixtures above, and for the same reason: reformatting them turns the next
# real measurement change into a diff nobody can read.
crates/*/tests/assets
